s custom upholstery products and eclectic looks, as well as offers mattress product lines under the Tempur-Pedic, Serta, Sealy, Beautyrest, and Stearns and Foster names. The company sells home furnishings through its retail stores, as well as through its website. Haverty Furniture Companies, Inc. was founded in 1885 and is headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Steven G. Burdette | President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $1.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $317K ranks in the below the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $14K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Haverty Furniture Companies, In is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $392M market cap on $759M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -10% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 32% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 22-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 54% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $33M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 4 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.67\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 15% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 89% leaves thin coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"amber","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 45% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Haverty Furniture Companies, Inc. $HVT Stock: Pzena Investment Management LLC Lowers Position","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/haverty-furniture-companies-inc-hvt-stock-pzena-investment-management-llc-lowers-position.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793876503.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.691,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Haverty Furniture Companies Inc (HVT) (Q3 2026) Earnings Call Highlights: Sales and Margins ...","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/haverty-furniture-companies-inc-hvt-030942670.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793848182.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Haverty Furniture (HVT) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/haverty-furniture-hvt-q3-2026-211618030.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793826978.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Havertys expects 2026 gross margins of 61.3% to 61.5% while planning 5 Q4 store openings (NYSE:HVT)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4665513-havertys-expects-2026-gross-margins-of-61_3-percent-to-61_5-percent-while-planning-5-q4-store","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793825834.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.372,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Haverty Furniture (HVT) Lags Q3 Earnings and Revenue Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3022683/haverty-furniture-hvt-lags-q3-earnings-and-revenue-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3022683","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793794203.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"titl